251 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Timing analysis is crucial in VLSI design to ensure that a circuit operates correctly under all conditions. There are two primary timing analysis methods: Static Timing Analysis \(STA\) and Dynamic Timing Analysis \(DTA\). While both techniques serve the purpose of verifying timing constraints, they have distinct methodologies, advantages, and limitations.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [15]
>>
